WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.652
Whoever's order waited in the book is the maker.

2
00:00:03.652 --> 00:00:07.367
Whoever took it is the taker, and the taker pays more.

3
00:00:07.367 --> 00:00:11.631
On spot the base fee is about one tenth of a percent per side,

4
00:00:11.631 --> 00:00:14.314
and a “buy — sell” round is two tenths.

5
00:00:14.314 --> 00:00:15.277
It seems tiny.

6
00:00:15.277 --> 00:00:20.918
But 500 rounds turn 100 dollars into about 37, without a single forecasting error.

7
00:00:21.918 --> 00:00:25.589
Hence a rule that honest testing confirms again and again:

8
00:00:25.589 --> 00:00:27.488
the more often an idea trades,

9
00:00:27.488 --> 00:00:30.906
the bigger the edge it needs just to pay for the fees.

10
00:00:30.906 --> 00:00:35.779
An idea that buys and sells with market orders every day loses about half its

11
00:00:35.779 --> 00:00:37.805
capital in a year on fees alone.

12
00:00:37.805 --> 00:00:41.286
That is why the program deducts costs from every trade.
